      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savona%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s first settlers arrived in 1793 when Thomas Corbitt built a sawmill and tavern near Mud Creek’s mouth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://savonaclerk.wixsite.com/mysite/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Savona sits where Mud Creek meets the Cohocton River, a historic confluence that helped shape early commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savona%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village was officially incorporated in 1883, marking its transition from a rural settlement to a formal municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savona%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Drivers pass through Savona at the crossroads of state routes 226 and 415, a junction that has guided travelers for generations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
